{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016cBsyV5d6Mwx4ZmBhS7XZy","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Write one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matching quote\nand a counter-search is refused. Paths are relative to the repo, which defaults to the\nfolder holding FINDINGS.json (set --repo to change it).\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nfrom validate_findings import quote_found, norm, refs  # noqa: E402\n\nCHECKS_FILE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"references\" / \"checks.json\"\n\n\ndef load(path):\n    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text())\n\n\ndef save(path, doc):\n    Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(doc, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef find_item(doc, item):\n    for f in doc[\"findings\"]:\n        if f[\"item\"] == item:\n            return f\n    sys.exit(f\"{item} isn't in this findings file.\")\n\n\ndef next_open(doc):\n    for f in doc[\"findings\"]:\n        for c in f.get(\"checks\", []):\n            if c.get(\"met\") == \"unknown\" and not norm(c.get(\"note\", \"\")):\n                return f\"Next: {c['id']} — {c.get('check', '')}\\n  How to verify: {c.get('verify', '')}\"\n        if str(f.get(\"summary\", \"\")).startswith(\"TODO\"):\n            return f\"Next: finish item {f['item']} with `answer.py ... item {f['item']} --rating ...`\"\n66:    ap.add_argument(\"findings\")\n67:    ap.add_argument(\"kind\", choices=[\"check\", \"flag\", \"item\", \"prescan\", \"next\"])\n68:    ap.add_argument(\"target\", nargs=\"?\")\n69:    ap.add_argument(\"--repo\")\n70:    ap.add_argument(\"--met\", choices=[\"yes\", \"no\", \"unknown\"])\n71:    ap.add_argument(\"--evidence\", default=\"\")\n72:    ap.add_argument(\"--quote\", default=\"\")\n73:    ap.add_argument(\"--counter\", default=\"\")\n74:    ap.add_argument(\"--note\", default=\"\")\n75:    ap.add_argument(\"--rating\", choices=[\"likely_pass\", \"gap\", \"needs_evidence\", \"na_candidate\"])\n76:    ap.add_argument(\"--confidence\", choices=[\"high\", \"medium\", \"low\"], default=\"medium\")\n77:    ap.add_argument(\"--summary\", default=\"\")\n78:    ap.add_argument(\"--next\", dest=\"next_step\", default=\"\")\n79:    ap.add_argument(\"--violates\", action=\"append\", default=[])\n80:    ap.add_argument(\"--also-affects\", action=\"append\", default=[])\n81:    ap.add_argument(\"--verdict\", choices=[\"confirmed\", \"dismissed\"])\n82:    ap.add_argument(\"--item\")\n83:    ap.add_argument(\"--reason\", default=\"\")\n225:1031-    \"verify\": \"1) Find the release manifest (`.brace/manifest.yaml`, release manifest, ML-BOM). 2) Check each category: container, harness, system prompt, rules files, model, built-in tools, MCP servers, permission scopes, memory and retrieval, identity bindings, network rules, budgets, security-policy versions. 3) Compare with what config sets up (`*.mcp.json`, NetworkPolicy). 4) Answer no if any category is missing or configured items are left out.\",\n344:1188-    \"verify\": \"1) Find the drift check job or tool. 2) List what it compares: images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, self-hosted weights. 3) Check each is compared with the approved baseline, not with the live state itself. 4) Answer no if any category is missing or excluded. Answer unknown if drift detection runs in an outside platform.\"\n377:1288-    \"verify\": \"1) List the test cases in the release suite. 2) Check each category exists: destructive-action denial, access limits, injection containment, audit attribution, stopping, plus retrieval, memory, and checker tests where those features exist. 3) Answer no if any category is missing or its tests are skipped (`skip`, `xfail`, excluded markers).\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6479d33-0daa-4375-b923-ca5308eb0272","uuid":"df69e491-9750-471d-ba7d-c0a3800cfb00","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:04:01.280Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Write one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matchi